Information
===========

This folder contains certificates and keys pertaining to code signing (scale features) and ssh keys.

Folder              Usage
------------------- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
./ca                Stores root certificate and issuing authorities. Don't use unless you know what your doing!
./ca/codeSigningCA  This is the issuing authority responsible for code signing.
./feature           Install script for scale feature.
./ssh               SSH key for root user.

There are also several certificates and scripts available.

Name                          Usage
----------------------------- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
copyCerts.sh                  Updates hobart code signing certificate and root cert. Use if you have generated a new certificate (i.e. the old one expired).
HobartCodeSigningCert.crt     Hobart code signing certificate and chain.
HobartCodeSigningCertKey.pem  Key file for the hobart certificate.
HobartRootCA.crt              Hobart root certificate.
signFeatureInstaller.sh       Generates signature for a file. This is a SHA256 sum, which is then signed with the private key.
verifyFeatureInstaller.sh     Validates a signature file using the hobart signing certificate.

If you have questions please see Randy.

Release Process
===============

The code signing certificate should be renewed every release. This process should be performed just before the release branch is taken. In this way, signed code is valid for 2 years. 

To generate a new certificate follow this process:

1) Generate a new CSR for this release

$ cd Windux/Application/certs/ca/codeSigningCA
$ CADIR=Windux/Application/certs/ca openssl req -config openssl.cnf \
      -key private/hobartkey.pem \
      -new -sha256 -out csr/hobartcsr-2.3.pem

Enter pass phrase for hobartkey.pem: authentichobart
You are about to be asked to enter information that will be incorporated
into your certificate request.
-----
Country Name (2 letter code) [US]:US
State or Province Name [Ohio]:Ohio
Locality Name [Troy]:Troy
Organization Name [ITW]:ITW
Organizational Unit Name [Hobart]:Hobart
Common Name []:Verified Hobart Software 2.3
Email Address []:HT.Support@itwfeg.com

Please enter the following 'extra' attributes
to be sent with your certificate request
A challenge password []:
An optional company name []:

2) Sign the CSR

$ CADIR=Windux/Application/certs/ca openssl ca -config openssl.cnf \
      -extensions usr_cert -days 730 -notext -md sha256 \
      -in csr/hobartcsr-2.3.pem \
      -out certs/hobartcert-2.3.pem
      
Enter pass phrase for intermediatekey.pem: code1signer

Sign the certificate? [y/n]:y
1 out of 1 certificate requests certified, commit? [y/n]y

3) Update the certs folder

$ cd Windux/Application/certs
$ gedit copyCerts.sh

Update the code signing cert to the one you just generated:

# generate code signing cert
cat ca/codeSigningCA/certs/hobartcert-2.3.pem ca/codeSigningCA/certs/intermediatecert.pem > $CRT

Save the script then run it.

$ ./copyCerts.sh

4) Add new files to SVN and check everything in

Make sure these files get added:
Windux/Application/certs/ca/codeSigningCA/newcerts/10XX.pem
Windux/Application/certs/ca/codeSigningCA/csr/hobartcsr-2.3.pem
Windux/Application/certs/ca/codeSigningCA/certs/hobartcert-2.3.pem

Do a check in.

New Code Signing Authority Process
==================================

This process should be performed every 5 years staring in 2015. So this means in years 2020, 2025, 2030, etc. Code signing authorities are valid for 10 years.

